# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 157-162 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 15 — CHAPTERS 17-18, LEAN, 2026-09-24): THE KING — a successor, not a queen, by a prophet, from
# the land and not the outsiders, his awe, a positive and a negative, no woman over the community, Agrippas weeping (157); horses for himself and not for the
# chariots, one idle horse and Egypt, the a fortiori of the covenant (158); eighteen wives, the wife who turns the heart, silver for the army, David and
# Solomon (159); the throne conditioned, his own copy, the copy of the whole, the scroll's skin and its correction by the seventy-one, the Torah forgotten
# (160); the copy with him everywhere, the nights, fear to Scripture to deed, the king's road, the statutes of kingship (161); not above the consecrated,
# right or left, long days conditioned, his sons and every provider's, Solomon's wealth (162). Every row READ WHOLE in both files. Sitting 14's form.
from ch17_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(157, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"SET, YOU SHALL SET" (17:15) — IF HE DIED, APPOINT ANOTHER IN HIS PLACE. The head row of piska 157 ({SP_(157, 1, "מת", "מנה", "אחר", "תחתיו")} "if he died, appoint another in his place"): the doubled verb read as SUCCESSION — the office continuous (162:4 the son): the compile\'s king a standing office, not a person. Fresh.')
srow(157, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"A KING" — AND NOT A QUEEN. ({SP_(157, 2, "מלך", "ולא", "מלכה")} "a king and not a queen"): the office male by the noun — a parameter of the compile\'s king (157:9 the community\'s provider likewise). Fresh.')
srow(157, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHOM THE LORD YOUR GOD WILL CHOOSE" — BY THE MOUTH OF A PROPHET. ({SP_(157, 3, "על", "פי", "נביא")} "by the mouth of a prophet"): THE KING\'S CHOICE THROUGH THE PROPHET — chapter 18\'s prophet the instrument of chapter 17\'s king (Samuel and Saul the run\'s case): the compile\'s king cell takes the prophet daemon\'s output as its selector. Fresh.')
srow(157, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"FROM AMONG" — AND NOT FROM OUTSIDE THE LAND. ({SP_(157, 4, "ולא", "מחוצה", "לארץ")} "and not from outside the land"): "from among your brothers" (one seat in the Bible, asserted) — the first exclusion the diaspora Israelite. Fresh.')
srow(157, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR BROTHERS" — AND NOT FROM OTHERS. ({SP_(157, 5, "ולא", "מאחרים")} "and not from others"): the second exclusion the gentile — "others" the word the English\'s note hears as "other gods". Fresh.')
srow(157, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL SET A KING OVER YOU" — WAS IT NOT ALREADY SAID "SET, YOU SHALL SET"? WHY "YOU SHALL SET A KING OVER YOU"? THAT HIS AWE BE UPON YOU. FROM HERE THEY SAID: A KING — NONE RIDE HIS HORSE, SIT ON HIS THRONE, USE HIS SCEPTRE, SEE HIM NAKED OR AT THE BARBER OR IN THE BATH. ({SP_(157, 6, "שתהא", "אימתו", "עליך")} "that his awe be upon you"; {SP_(157, 6, "אין", "רוכבים", "על", "סוסו")} "none ride his horse"): THE KING\'S AWE from the repeated clause — Mishnah Sanhedrin 2:5\'s six rules (the "from here they said" without a name): the compile\'s king carries an honor parameter with six bars. Fresh.')
srow(157, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "SET, YOU SHALL SET A KING OVER YOU" — A POSITIVE COMMANDMENT. ({SP_(157, 7, "מצות", "עשה")} "a positive commandment"): the king an obligation (156:5\'s arm). Fresh.')
srow(157, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU MAY NOT SET OVER YOU A FOREIGNER" — A NEGATIVE COMMANDMENT. ({SP_(157, 8, "מצות", "לא", "תעשה")} "a negative commandment"): the foreigner\'s bar — ONKELOS "you have no permission" (the book\'s four seats, asserted): the compile\'s two effects on the one appointment. Fresh.')
srow(157, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"A FOREIGN MAN" — FROM HERE THEY SAID: A MAN IS APPOINTED PROVIDER OVER THE COMMUNITY, A WOMAN IS NOT. ({SP_(157, 9, "האיש", "ממנים", "פרנס", "על", "הצבור")} "a man they appoint provider over the community"): "man" read past the king to EVERY COMMUNAL OFFICE — the compile\'s office parameter generalized (162:4 the providers\' sons). Fresh.')
srow(157, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'(MISHNAH SOTAH 7:8) "WHO IS NOT YOUR BROTHER" — WHEN AGRIPPAS REACHED THIS VERSE HE WEPT, AND ALL ISRAEL SAID TO HIM: FEAR NOT, AGRIPPAS, YOU ARE OUR BROTHER, YOU ARE OUR BROTHER! ({SP_(157, 10, "כשהיה", "אגריפס", "מגיע", "לפסוק", "זה", "היה", "בוכה")} "when Agrippas reached this verse he would weep"; {SP_(157, 10, "אחינו", "אתה", "אחינו", "אתה")} "you are our brother, you are our brother"): THE MISHNAH CITED IN THE HEBREW ITSELF — the king\'s reading on the assembly day (31:10-13 ahead) meeting his own disqualification: the run\'s case of a king by a foreign line, the verse read aloud by its subject. Fresh.')
srow(158, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"ONLY HE SHALL NOT MULTIPLY HORSES FOR HIMSELF" (17:16) — MIGHT HE NOT MULTIPLY FOR HIS CHARIOTS AND HORSEMEN? THE TEACHING SAYS "FOR HIMSELF" — FOR HIMSELF NOT, BUT FOR HIS CHARIOTS AND HORSEMEN HE MAY. The head row of piska 158 ({SP_(158, 1, "לו", "אינו", "מרבה")} "for himself he does not multiply"; {SP_(158, 1, "אבל", "מרבה", "הוא", "למרכבתו", "ולפרשיו")} "but he multiplies for his chariots and his horsemen"): THE FIRST LIMIT SPLIT BY "FOR HIMSELF" — the army\'s horses allowed, the king\'s own barred (Sanhedrin 2:4): the compile\'s horse parameter two-valued. Fresh.')
srow(158, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'IF SO, WHY "IN ORDER TO MULTIPLY HORSE"? IDLE HORSES. ({SP_(158, 2, "סוסים", "בטלים")} "idle horses"): the singular "horse" (asserted the verse\'s two forms) read as the idle beast — the bar on horses with no use. Fresh.')
srow(158, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT EVEN ONE IDLE HORSE IS ENOUGH TO RETURN THE PEOPLE TO EGYPT? "ONLY HE SHALL NOT MULTIPLY HORSES … AND SHALL NOT RETURN". ({SP_(158, 3, "אפלו", "סוס", "אחד", "והוא", "בטל")} "even one horse and it is idle"; {SP_(158, 3, "שיחזיר", "את", "העם", "למצרים")} "that he return the people to Egypt"): ONE HORSE THE THRESHOLD — the verse\'s reason ("lest he return the people to Egypt") read as the bar\'s measure: the compile\'s limit not a count but a purpose; Solomon\'s horses from Egypt the run\'s case (1 Kings 10:28 — no token shared, asserted). Fresh.')
srow(158, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'IS IT NOT AN A FORTIORI? IF EGYPT, ON WHICH THE COVENANT IS CUT, A TRANSGRESSION RETURNS THEM THERE — THE OTHER LANDS, ON WHICH NO COVENANT IS CUT, HOW MUCH MORE. ({SP_(158, 4, "שהברית", "כרותה", "עליה")} "on which the covenant is cut"; {SP_(158, 4, "על", "אחת", "כמה", "וכמה")} "how much more"): I1 (the a fortiori; checked in MIDDOT.md) from Egypt\'s sworn return to every land\'s (the row without a citation) — 28:68\'s ships ahead: the compile\'s exile effect a consequence of the king\'s horses. Fresh.')
srow(159, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE SHALL NOT MULTIPLY WIVES FOR HIMSELF" (17:17) — BUT EIGHTEEN. The head row of piska 159 ({SP_(159, 1, "אלא", "שמונה", "עשרה")} "but eighteen"): THE SECOND LIMIT A NUMBER — eighteen (Sanhedrin 2:4 from David\'s wives, 2 Samuel 12:8 the segment\'s count): the compile\'s wives parameter 18. Fresh.')
srow(159, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JUDAH: HE MAY MULTIPLY, PROVIDED THEY DO NOT TURN HIS HEART. ({SP_(159, 2, "מרבה", "הוא", "לו")} "he may multiply for himself"; {SP_(159, 2, "מסירות", "את", "לבו")} "turn his heart"): the number waived for the REASON — the verse\'s "lest his heart turn" the rule\'s whole content (the row without a citation): the dispute\'s second arm. Fresh.')
srow(159, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SIMEON: EVEN ONE WHO TURNS HIS HEART HE SHALL NOT MARRY; THEN WHY "HE SHALL NOT MULTIPLY WIVES"? EVEN LIKE ABIGAIL — EVEN ABIGAIL AND HER COMPANIONS WHO ARE FIT; AND LIKE JEZEBEL AND HERS WHO ARE WICKED, SHE TURNS HIS HEART. ({SP_(159, 3, "אפלו", "אחת", "והיא", "מסירה", "את", "לבו")} "even one, and she turns his heart"; {SP_(159, 3, "אפלו", "כאביגיל")} "even like Abigail"): the third arm — the number and the reason both (Sanhedrin 2:4 the sheet; the English\'s note: redundant in many versions); Abigail and Jezebel the run\'s cases: the compile\'s wives cell three-armed. Fresh.')
srow(159, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND SILVER AND GOLD HE SHALL NOT MULTIPLY GREATLY" — MIGHT HE NOT MULTIPLY TO PAY THE ARMY? "FOR HIMSELF" — FOR HIMSELF NOT, BUT FOR THE ARMY HE MAY; SO DAVID DID (1 CHRONICLES 22:14) BUT SOLOMON CHANGED IT, "HE MADE SILVER IN JERUSALEM AS STONES" (1 KINGS 10:27). ({SP_(159, 4, "כדי", "לתן", "לאפסניא")} "in order to give to the army"; {SP_(159, 4, "אבל", "שלמה", "שנה")} "but Solomon changed"): THE THIRD LIMIT SPLIT BY "FOR HIMSELF" like the first (Sanhedrin 2:4) — DAVID KEPT IT, SOLOMON BROKE IT (the run\'s cases; 17:17 shares nothing in order with 1 Kings 10:27, asserted): the compile\'s treasury parameter two-valued, the tape\'s kings graded. Fresh.')
srow(160, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND IT SHALL BE WHEN HE SITS ON THE THRONE OF HIS KINGDOM" (17:18) — IF HE DOES ALL SAID IN THE MATTER, HE IS WORTHY TO SIT ON THE THRONE OF HIS KINGDOM. The head row of piska 160 ({SP_(160, 1, "כדי", "הוא", "שישב", "על", "כסא", "ממלכתו")} "he is worthy to sit on the throne of his kingdom"): the throne CONDITIONED on the limits (the trope of 156:1, 162:3) — the compile\'s reign an effect gated on the three bars. Fresh.')
srow(160, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE SHALL WRITE FOR HIMSELF" — FOR HIS OWN NAME, THAT HE NOT USE HIS FATHERS\'. ({SP_(160, 2, "לשמו")} "for his name"; {SP_(160, 2, "שלא", "יהא", "נאות", "בשל", "אבותיו")} "that he not benefit from his fathers\'"): THE COPY HIS OWN, never inherited (Tosefta Sanhedrin 4:7) — the compile\'s copy effect written per king. Fresh.')
srow(160, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"A COPY" — ONLY THE COPY OF THE LAW (DEUTERONOMY)? THE REST OF THE TORAH — WHENCE? "TO KEEP ALL THE WORDS OF THIS LAW AND THESE STATUTES" (17:19). THEN WHY "THE COPY OF THE LAW"? BECAUSE IT WAS TO BE CHANGED. ({SP_(160, 3, "אין", "לי", "אלא", "משנה", "תורה")} "I have only the copy of the law"; {SP_(160, 3, "שעתידה", "להשתנות")} "that it was to be changed"): "THE COPY OF THIS LAW" (one seat, asserted) read first as the book\'s own name and then as the whole Torah — and "copy" as "change": the script to be changed (Tosefta Sanhedrin 4:7\'s Assyrian script, the English\'s note): the compile\'s copy the whole law, its script a parameter of the era. Fresh.')
srow(160, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'OTHERS SAY: ON THE ASSEMBLY DAY THEY READ ONLY THE COPY OF THE LAW. ({SP_(160, 4, "אין", "קוראים", "ביום", "הקהל", "אלא", "משנה", "תורה", "בלבד")} "they read on the assembly day only the copy of the law"): the book\'s name kept for the reading of 31:10-13 (ahead) — the king\'s reading Deuteronomy alone (157:10\'s Agrippas): the compile\'s assembly-day parameter. Fresh.')
srow(160, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"ON A BOOK" — NOT ON A TABLET; "ON A BOOK" — NOT ON PAPER, BUT ON A SCROLL, AS IT IS SAID "ON A BOOK". ({SP_(160, 5, "ולא", "על", "הלוח")} "and not on a tablet"; {SP_(160, 5, "ולא", "על", "הניר")} "and not on paper"; {SP_(160, 5, "אלא", "על", "המגלה")} "but on a scroll"): THE MEDIUM A SCROLL — ONKELOS "the scroll" (ten seats in the book, asserted): the compile\'s copy a material parameter. Fresh.')
srow(160, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"FROM BEFORE THE PRIESTS THE LEVITES" — THAT IT BE CORRECTED FROM BEFORE THE PRIESTS THE LEVITES. ({SP_(160, 6, "שתהא", "מגהת", "מלפני", "הכהנים", "הלוים")} "that it be corrected from before the priests the Levites"): the priests the PROOFREADERS (Tosefta Sanhedrin 4:7) — the compile\'s copy validated against the priests\' text. Fresh.')
srow(160, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"ON A BOOK" — ON THE SKIN OF A CLEAN BEAST; AND THEY CORRECT IT FROM THE COURTYARD\'S SCROLL BY THE COURT OF SEVENTY-ONE. ({SP_(160, 7, "על", "גבי", "עור", "בהמה", "טהורה")} "on the skin of a clean beast"; {SP_(160, 7, "מספר", "עזרה", "על", "פי", "בית", "דין", "של", "שבעים", "ואחד")} "from the courtyard\'s scroll by the court of seventy-one"): THE MASTER COPY IN THE COURTYARD and the great court its keeper (14b\'s ES_SIZES 71) — the compile\'s copy checked against the place\'s text by the high court: the two daemons joined at the scroll. Fresh.')
srow(160, 8, 'CONTEXT', f'"FROM BEFORE THE PRIESTS THE LEVITES" — FROM HERE R. ELAZAR BEN ARAKH EXPOUNDED THAT THE TORAH WAS DESTINED TO BE FORGOTTEN. ({SP_(160, 8, "שסוף", "תורה", "עתידה", "להשתכח")} "that the Torah was destined to be forgotten"): the priests\' keeping read as a prophecy of loss (Tosefta Eduyot 1:1) — the context of 160:6. Fresh.')
srow(161, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND IT SHALL BE WITH HIM AND HE SHALL READ IN IT ALL THE DAYS OF HIS LIFE" (17:19) — FROM HERE THEY SAID (MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 2:4): THE KING GOES OUT TO WAR AND IT IS WITH HIM, COMES IN AND IT IS WITH HIM, SITS IN JUDGMENT AND IT IS BESIDE HIM, RECLINES AND IT IS BEFORE HIM. The head row of piska 161 ({SP_(161, 1, "יוצא", "למלחמה", "והוא", "עמו")} "goes out to war and it is with him"; {SP_(161, 1, "מסב", "והוא", "כנגדו")} "reclines and it is before him"): THE MISHNAH CITED IN THE HEBREW ITSELF — "with him" in four scenes (war, return, judgment, the table): the compile\'s copy a companion state on every king\'s act. Fresh.')
srow(161, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE DAYS OF HIS LIFE" — THE DAYS; "ALL THE DAYS OF HIS LIFE" — THE NIGHTS. ({SP_(161, 2, "ימי", "חייו", "הימים")} "the days of his life — the days"; {SP_(161, 2, "הלילות")} "the nights"): "ALL" WIDENS TO THE NIGHTS — Berakhot 1:5\'s own reading (ben Zoma\'s "all" at chapter 16\'s 130:7, the same move): the compile\'s reading clock day and night. Fresh.')
srow(161, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT HE MAY LEARN TO FEAR THE LORD HIS GOD" — TEACHES THAT FEAR BRINGS TO SCRIPTURE, SCRIPTURE TO TRANSLATION, TRANSLATION TO MISHNAH, MISHNAH TO TALMUD, TALMUD TO DEED, DEED TO FEAR. SINCE THE COMMONER EQUALS THE KING IN WORDS OF TORAH, MIGHT HE EQUAL HIM IN OTHER THINGS? "TO KEEP ALL THE WORDS OF THIS LAW" — IN WORDS OF TORAH HE EQUALS HIM, NOT IN OTHER THINGS. ({SP_(161, 3, "שהמורא", "מביא", "לידי", "מקרא")} "that fear brings to Scripture"; {SP_(161, 3, "מעשה", "מביא", "לידי", "יראה")} "deed brings to fear"; {SP_(161, 3, "ששוה", "הדיוט", "למלך", "בדברי", "תורה")} "that the commoner equals the king in words of Torah"): THE CIRCLE OF LEARNING in six steps closing on itself (fear → Scripture → translation → Mishnah → Talmud → deed → fear) — the shelf\'s own ladder named inside the spine; the king and the commoner equal in Torah alone: the compile\'s king shares the learning effect with every Israelite and nothing else. Fresh.')
srow(161, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'FROM HERE THEY SAID (MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 2:4): A KING BREAKS THROUGH TO MAKE HIMSELF A ROAD AND NONE PROTEST, WIDENS HIS ROADS AND NONE PROTEST; THE KING\'S ROAD HAS NO MEASURE, AND ALL THE PEOPLE PLUNDER AND SET IT BEFORE HIM AND HE TAKES THE FIRST SHARE. ({SP_(161, 4, "מלך", "פורץ", "לעשות", "לו", "דרך")} "a king breaks through to make himself a road"; {SP_(161, 4, "והוא", "נוטל", "חלק", "בראש")} "and he takes the first share"): THE MISHNAH CITED IN THE HEBREW A SECOND TIME IN THE PISKA — the king\'s "other things" (Sanhedrin 2:4, Bava Batra 6:7): the road without measure and the first share of the spoil: the compile\'s king rights three effects on the land and the spoil ledgers. Fresh.')
srow(161, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AND THESE STATUTES" — THESE ARE THE STATUTES OF KINGSHIP. ({SP_(161, 5, "אלה", "חקי", "מלכות")} "these are the statutes of kingship"): "these statutes" read as THE KING\'S OWN LAW (the row without a citation; 160:3\'s "these statutes" the whole Torah) — a second reading: the compile keeps both as the statute set\'s two scopes. Fresh.')
srow(162, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT HIS HEART BE NOT LIFTED ABOVE HIS BROTHERS" (17:20) — AND NOT ABOVE THE CONSECRATED. The head row of piska 162 ({SP_(162, 1, "ולא", "משל", "הקדש")} "and not above what is the sanctuary\'s"): the king\'s heart barred from rising over the PRIESTHOOD too (the English\'s note: the high priest) — "his heart lifted" one seat (asserted): the compile\'s king below the sanctuary\'s office. Fresh.')
srow(162, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THAT HE TURN NOT FROM THE COMMANDMENT RIGHT OR LEFT" — THAT HE NOT TURN FROM THE COMMANDMENT RIGHT OR LEFT. ({SP_(162, 2, "שלא", "יסור", "מן", "המצוה", "ימין", "ושמאול")} "that he not turn from the commandment right or left"): the archaic "lest" rendered in the sages\' Hebrew — the spelling here FULL (17:20 with 28:14; 17:11 defective, asserted): the king under 17:11\'s court clause with the other spelling. Fresh.')
srow(162, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT HE MAY PROLONG DAYS OVER HIS KINGDOM" — IF HE DOES WHAT IS WRITTEN IN THE MATTER, HE IS WORTHY TO PROLONG DAYS OVER HIS KINGDOM. ({SP_(162, 3, "כדי", "הוא", "שיאריך", "ימים", "על", "ממלכתו")} "he is worthy to prolong days over his kingdom"): the reign\'s length CONDITIONED (160:1\'s trope) — "prolong days" the Torah\'s one seat of the Bible\'s four (asserted): the compile\'s reign-length effect gated. Fresh.')
srow(162, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"HE AND HIS SONS" — IF HE DIED, HIS SON STANDS IN HIS PLACE. ONLY THE KING? WHENCE EVERY PROVIDER OF ISRAEL, THAT THEIR SONS STAND IN THEIR PLACE? "HE AND HIS SONS IN THE MIDST OF ISRAEL" — WHOEVER IS IN THE MIDST OF ISRAEL, HIS SON STANDS IN HIS PLACE. ({SP_(162, 4, "שאם", "מת", "בנו", "עומד", "תחתיו")} "that if he died his son stands in his place"; {SP_(162, 4, "לכל", "פרנסי", "ישראל")} "to every provider of Israel"): SUCCESSION BY THE SON for the king and EVERY OFFICE (Tosefta Shekalim 2:15; 157:9\'s provider) — the compile\'s office succession a general rule. Fresh.')
srow(162, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'R. HANANIAH BEN GAMLIEL: "ALSO WHAT YOU DID NOT ASK I HAVE GIVEN YOU, RICHES AND HONOR" (1 KINGS 3:13) — WHAT I DID NOT CONDITION IN THE TORAH I GAVE; WHAT I CONDITIONED I GIVE ONLY IF YOU DO — "AND IF YOU WALK IN MY WAYS" (3:14). ({SP_(162, 5, "על", "מה", "שלא", "התניתי", "בתורה", "לתן")} "for what I did not condition in the Torah to give"): Solomon\'s unasked gifts against the conditioned length of days — the run\'s case (17:20 shares nothing in order with 1 Kings 3:14, asserted): the conditioned and the free rewards two classes on the tape. Fresh.')
